{
  "id": 22,
  "name": "lookahead_return_v3",
  "intent": "Adds an explicit 2-step lookahead via a nearest_remaining penalty, discouraging isolated candidates whose best next unvisited is far. This complements the parent's regret bonus (gap between best and 2nd-best next step) by penalizing absolute future cost, not just relative gap. Return penalty ramps faster with progress (0.15 to 0.50) to tighten late-stage closure on long edges. Cluster density stays low-weighted because it's noisy on flat (uniform/grid) topologies where the parent is weakest. Distance remains dominant. Targets reducing forced long jumps in grid/uniform while preserving clustered performance.",
  "tags": [
    "lookahead",
    "return_aware"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    dist = f['distance']\n    ret = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    reg = f['regret']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    prog = f['progress']\n    rw = 0.15 + 0.35 * prog\n    rp = rw * ret\n    np = 0.20 * nr\n    rb = 0.25 * reg\n    db = 0.05 * cd\n    return -dist + rp + np + rb + db",
  "source": "live_llm",
